# Module documentation (backend + frontend)

When you **create or meaningfully change** a first-party module under `backend/Modules/*` or `frontend/src/modules/*`:

## Required artifacts

1. **`README.md`** in the module root (BE and FE separately if both exist)
   - Purpose, quick path map, permissions/gates, runtime deps (if any)
   - Links to `docs/extensions/*.md` or architecture docs when relevant
   - Short “Agent notes” (do/don’t for the next agent)
2. **`CHANGELOG.md`** in the same module root
   - Keep a Changelog style; put new entries under `[Unreleased]`
   - Move to a dated/versioned section when the work ships/merges

## Also update

- Extension/product doc if one exists (e.g. `docs/extensions/ja-mail.md`)
- Root `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` with a one-line pointer for user-visible releases

## Do not

- Leave hanging “future backlog” items that belong to other systems (e.g. MTA/DNS/IMAP for JA-Mail)
- Skip changelog when behavior, API, or permissions change
